WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.220
- [Narrator] In addition
to citizenship rights,

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:08.220
citizens also have
responsibilities and obligations.

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:13.190
Now obligations are those
activities that citizens must do,

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:16.370
or they'll face legal repercussions.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:20.670
But responsibilities are
activities that citizens should do

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:24.090
to be good and productive
members of society.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.010
So you won't get in trouble
with the law if you don't do

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:30.240
them, but your community
will be a better place

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.910
if you do.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:34.900
We'll talk more about the
obligations of citizenship

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.180
in another video.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.573
So for now, let's just focus
on the responsibilities.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.400
What are those responsibilities?

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.780
First there's voting.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:49.520
It's not legally required
that citizens vote

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.030
in the United States,

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:54.050
unlike in some other countries
where citizens can get

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:56.130
in trouble, if they don't vote.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:59.830
But responsible citizens get
involved with the decision

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:00.709
making process, through voting.

00:01:00.709 --> 00:01:04.350
And to be a good voter,

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.690
It's important that citizens are informed.

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:10.970
They stay up to date on the
issues that government is facing

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.990
and they research candidates
and ballot measures

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.343
before they vote.

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:20.500
the voting, isn't the only way
to be a responsible citizen.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:23.743
You can also do so by
voicing your concerns.

00:01:27.598 --> 00:01:31.502
For example, something I did
recently, and this is true,

00:01:31.502 --> 00:01:32.335
was emailing my city's transit
department about a street

00:01:35.071 --> 00:01:37.841
light that wasn't functioning
properly near where I live,

00:01:37.841 --> 00:01:40.192
the transit department
came out and fixed it.

00:01:40.192 --> 00:01:41.025
And now there's less of a
chance that an accident will

00:01:41.025 --> 00:01:42.420
happen in that intersection.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:46.010
So when you notice a problem
that may affect others,

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:50.310
it's responsible to speak
up and try to fix things.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:54.410
You can also act as a responsible
citizen by volunteering.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:57.500
If you have a skill to
teach others or time to give

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.890
for a good cause you can make
your community a better place

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:02.870
through your service.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:03.800
Lastly,

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:08.320
good citizens respect the
rights and beliefs of others.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:10.750
They understand that in a democracy,

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.960
not everyone may have the
same opinions or concerns

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:16.870
as they do, but everyone else is entitled

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:19.213
to the same rights as they are.

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:22.670
So that's a quick rundown of

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:25.250
the responsibilities of citizenship.

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:27.980
Which one do you think is most important?

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.833
What other things can you do
to improve your community?

